== Notes ==
* When thrown onto the ground, Refined eitr will emit occasional sparks that deal 30 [[Damage#Poison|poison]] and 30 [[Damage#Lightning|lightning]] damage in the same way that the Eitr refinery does while it is in operation. These sparks can damage anything NOT immune to those types of damage, including creatures and other structures.
* After acquiring some, the player can drop several Refined eitr near [[Dvergr Component Crate]]s for the resulting sparks to destroy them and claim more [[Dvergr Extractor|extractors]]. This process will not anger the nearby Dvergr, even if a Ward is present. Alternatively, it can be used to destroy the Ward itself and then manually attack the crate.

